-- I37 (#3678) S2-DECL (d): a point-free top-level binding (`g = mth`) of an
-- imported standalone `mth` while two interfaces declaring `mth` are admitted (each
-- named in its own import clause), with `amodI` before `zmodI`.  A value occurrence
-- applies no argument, so neither declaration's receiver can be evaluated there and the
-- two have not been shown to agree: the located `T-AMBIGUOUS-SHADOW-DECL` at the
-- occurrence, on every verb and in both import orders.  `impl IA String` (55) and
-- `impl IZ String` (7) make the two declarations disagree at a `String` receiver, so
-- binding the standalone (99) is a wrong answer, not a harmless pick.
import fmodI.{mth}
import amodI.{IA, af}
import zmodI.{IZ, zf}

g : String -> Int -> Int
g = mth

main = println (g "abc" 5 + af 0 + zf 0)
